## Additional Attribution

This repository contains a modernized reimplementation of the deep learning pipeline for
pacemaker detection in ECG signals, based on research conducted in collaboration between:

- **AI Center for Cardiology, Sheba Medical Center** (Israel)
- **Philips Research North America**

### Original Researchers (Sheba Medical Center)
- Dvora Rothman
- Elisheva Tufik
- Sigal Sina
- Gal Goshen
- Raizy Kellerman
- Michal Cohen-Shelly
- Avi Sabbag

### Philips Research North America Contributors
- Sara Mariani
- Annamalai Natarajan
- Asif Rahman
- Yale Chang
- Jonathan Rubin
- Shruti Vij
- Gregory Boverman

### Original Data Sources
- PhysioNet 2020 Challenge datasets (BSD 2-Clause)
- PTB-XL ECG Database
- Private annotated data from Sheba Medical Center (used with permission, **not redistributed**)

### Conference Presentation
This work was presented as a poster at the **Israel Cardiology Association Conference** (May 2025).

### Portfolio Adaptation
This repository has been adapted for portfolio demonstration by **Yazan Al-Jabari**.
- All real patient data has been removed
- Synthetic data generator added for demonstration
- Dependencies modernized for current Python/PyTorch versions
- Docker environment updated to CUDA 12.1

**No real patient data is included in this repository.** The synthetic data generator
creates realistic-looking but entirely artificial ECG signals for demonstration purposes.